Negative control for the table as the FRAME during loading (C8).

Restores the whole-surface loading notice, so the table — headers included —
is swapped out while the rows load and the layout jumps when they land. The
"loading state is awful" defect, exactly.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the loading-state specs — the real headers stay rendered with skeleton
rows beneath them.

